---
<section class="app-section">
  <p class="eyebrow">Built for the ride</p>
  <h2>Everything you need at a glance. Nothing you don&rsquo;t.</h2>
  <ul class="features">
    <li>
      <h3>Readable in full sun</h3>
      <p>Big, high-contrast numbers you can read with one glance, even with the screen dimmed.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <h3>Radar alerts</h3>
      <p>Pair a Garmin Varia and see vehicles approaching from behind before you hear them.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <h3>Your sensors, your zones</h3>
      <p>Connects to Bluetooth heart rate, speed, and cadence sensors. HR zones are set from your Apple Health data.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <h3>Personalizable Dashboard</h3>
      <p>Easily customize your dashboard to show the metrics that matter most to you.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <h3>Routes and Directions</h3>
      <p>Create, import, and save custom routes, and get turn-by-turn directions for your rides, all included in the app.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <h3>Integrated Weather</h3>
      <p>Real-time weather updates and forecasts right in the app, so you can plan your rides accordingly.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <h3>Native iPhone</h3>
      <p>Optimized for the iPhone, with a seamless integration to Apple services such as Apple Health, making every interaction feel natural and intuitive.</p>
    </li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="app-section">
  <p class="eyebrow">Private by design</p>
  <h2>Your rides stay on your iPhone.</h2>
  <ul class="features">
    <li>
      <h3>No login required</h3>
      <p>No sign-up, no login, no backend. Open the app and ride. Connect to the services and devices you trust. Everything is stored locally on your device.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <h3>On-device history</h3>
      <p>Routes, heart rate, and ride history are stored only on your phone, and nothing is sold or shared for advertising.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <h3>Share on your terms</h3>
      <p>Completed rides can be saved to Apple Health, and you can export any ride as a GPX file.</p>
    </li>
  </ul>
</section>
